From 9e40e72d59da9d1c267f2845cec97960971509b7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dan Brickley <danbri@danbri.org>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 13:52:27 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] mod_mix: serve the MIX information node and preserve the PAM
 namespace

Problem and evidence:

Two gaps were observed against ejabberd 26.07 (commit 413e7fa) with the
bundled xmpp codec 1.13.4. First, mod_mix negotiated only the messages and
participants nodes and answered a PubSub items request for
urn:xmpp:mix:nodes:info with feature-not-implemented, although current
clients request the info node during join and read it during discovery.
Second, mod_mix_pam built the client-join result with the namespace taken
from the channel's inner join reply (urn:xmpp:mix:core:1) instead of the
namespace of the client's own request (urn:xmpp:mix:pam:2). Both were
reproduced with a raw loopback client and match the report in ejabberd
issue 4006, which its reporter closed in 2023 without a fix.

Protocol expectation:

XEP-0369 version 0.14.6 section 6.1 lists urn:xmpp:mix:nodes:info as a
standard node, shows it being read through PubSub during channel discovery
before a join, and shows it in the join subscription list. Its item is an
XEP-0004 form with FORM_TYPE urn:xmpp:mix:core:1 and Name, Description and
Contact fields. XEP-0405 requires the client-join result to be in the
urn:xmpp:mix:pam:2 namespace the client used.

Change:

- Add urn:xmpp:mix:nodes:info to known_nodes/0, so a join that asks for it
  receives it in the negotiated subscription list.
- Answer a PubSub items request for the info node with one item, id
  "current", holding the form built by info_node_form/2. The form carries
  FORM_TYPE, Name (the channel localpart) and Contact (the channel creator).
  Description is omitted because this module stores no description.
- A channel that is not hidden answers any requester, as in the discovery
  flow. A hidden channel answers only participants, matching the way the
  hidden flag already restricts disco#items. Unknown channels and database
  failures return the same errors as the participants node.
- mod_mix_pam threads the client's PAM namespace through to the result
  instead of reusing the channel reply's namespace.
- No change to the -protocol attribute, channel creation, messages,
  participants, MAM, or routing.

Status-quo compatibility:

Before: info-node requests failed with feature-not-implemented and a join
requesting the info node was silently narrowed to messages and participants;
the client-join result carried urn:xmpp:mix:core:1. After: the info node is
served and negotiated and the result carries urn:xmpp:mix:pam:2. Joins that
never mention the info node, and every other node, behave as before.

Interoperability and operational risks:

Clients that never request the info node see no change. A client that
compared the client-join result namespace against urn:xmpp:mix:core:1
would now fail, but XEP-0405 does not permit that expectation and no such
client is known. The info node exposes the creator's bare JID to any user
who can already discover the channel; hidden channels are unchanged in
visibility. No archive, persistence, multi-resource, or routing effect.
Rollback is a single-patch revert with no database migration.

Verification:

EUnit test/mod_mix_info_test.erl: the info node is negotiable, existing
nodes remain negotiable, the form is typed urn:xmpp:mix:core:1, carries
Name and a jid-multi Contact, and round-trips through the xmpp codec.
Result on Erlang/OTP 29: 5 tests, 0 failures. The series applies cleanly
to the pinned upstream commit with git am. Earlier revisions of this
patch (Name-only form, participants-only access) ran in the loopback pilot
with BeagleIM 6.0.1 and the browser client joining through PAM 2/Core 1
with the info node in the subscription list. The current form and the
discovery-read path are verified by a raw loopback probe against the
container image built from this series; see docs/0001-info-node.md for
the probe record.
